# ==============================================================================
# KisanLink AI — Environment Configuration (.env)
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env in the project root:
#   copy .env.example .env
#
# 1. DATABASE CONFIGURATION:
# By default, KisanLink uses the local SQLite datastore (backend/kisanlink.db).
# To connect a live PostgreSQL instance, uncomment and set DATABASE_URL below:
#
# Local PostgreSQL:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:yourpassword@localhost:5432/kisanlink
#
# Free Cloud PostgreSQL (e.g. Neon, Supabase, Render, Railway):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://neondb_owner:npg_xyz@ep-cold-lake-123.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
# 2. RUNNING THE POSTGRESQL MIGRATION:
# Once DATABASE_URL is set, migrate data from SQLite to PostgreSQL by running:
#   python backend/migrate_postgres.py
#
# 3. GOVERNMENT DATA INGESTION (data.gov.in):
# Optional API key for live Agmarknet APMC feeds:
# DATA_GOV_IN_API_KEY=579b464db66ec23bdd000001cdd3946e44ce4aad7209ff7b23ac571b
# ==============================================================================
